{"case_id":"T8011","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry point","API protocol","state","input semantics","attack surface"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["archive_read_open_filenames","archive_read_set_switch_callback","archive_read_set_callback_data2","archive_read_add_callback_data","archive_read_append_callback_data","archive_read_prepend_callback_data","archive_read_open1","client_switch_proxy","client_close_proxy","__archive_read_filter_ahead","advance_file_pointer","file_open","file_switch","file_close"],"reason":"S1 introduces multivolume archive input through archive_read_open_filenames and a new callback-data protocol built around client.dataset, client.nodes, client.cursor, and archive_switch_callback. H0 exclusively calls archive_read_open_memory(a, image, size) with one contiguous buffer, so it cannot select the new entry point, construct multiple data nodes, control volume boundaries, exercise switching when a read returns zero, or test close/open fallback versus file_switch. This is a material commit-induced coverage gap because these externally controllable volume sequences and transition states did not exist in S0.","evidence":["archive.h adds the public entry point archive_read_open_filenames and the public APIs archive_read_set_switch_callback, archive_read_set_callback_data2, archive_read_add_callback_data, archive_read_append_callback_data, and archive_read_prepend_callback_data.","archive_read_client replaces the single client.data field with nodes, cursor, dataset, and switcher, creating new multi-object state and callback sequencing.","__archive_read_filter_ahead and advance_file_pointer now call client_switch_proxy when the current reader returns zero and client.cursor is not client.nodes - 1.","client_switch_proxy either invokes client.switcher with the old and new data objects or performs the new closer-then-opener fallback protocol.","archive_read_open_filenames builds one read_file_data object per filename and installs file_switch, so filename count, ordering, empty termination, and boundaries affect parsing behavior.","H0 configures filters and formats but supplies fuzzed bytes only through archive_read_open_memory; it never calls any newly added multivolume or callback-data API and exposes no control over nodes, cursor, dataset, or switch transitions."],"recommended_action":"Extend the harness with a mode that partitions fuzz input into multiple independently controlled volumes and opens them through archive_read_open_filenames or the callback-data APIs. Vary volume count, ordering, empty/truncated volumes, split positions, switch return codes, and switcher-present versus closer/opener fallback while continuing header and data-block iteration."}
